// axis-bridge-world.axreg -- the W1 world layer (axMachina v2 codegen layer, axm-req-r99, 2026-10-09).
// Effects are slots to the outer world; the code between them stays pure. Every w_ fn goes through one switch
// (AX_WORLD = real | record:<file> | replay:<file>, axis-codegen-bridge-rs src/runtime/world.rs) and returns a
// result instead of panicking ("Ok:..." / "Err:<reason>"; w_run a record (exit, stdout, stderr)). w_get / w_set
// are in-process state, never recorded. A new layer: legacy fns are untouched, and a build sees these names only
// when it passes this file (--reg) and axis-bridge-world.dispatch.toml (--dispatch to the bridge). Resource and
// key argument per fn: axis-bridge-world.effects.tsv. Identities are sha256(name) (§5b).
